-lens verification contracts","tree":{"sha":"4fb915a9e1656f0108a374a4db1aa83dba9a30c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/trees/4fb915a9e1656f0108a374a4db1aa83dba9a30c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/commits/0faf606a131133e050b2b599b5d0cdf75e545c6e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/0faf606a131133e050b2b599b5d0cdf75e545c6e","html_url":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/elenchus/commit/0faf606a131133e050b2b599b5d0cdf75e545c6e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/0faf606a131133e050b2b599b5d0cdf75e545c6e/comments","author":{"login":"codex","id":267193182,"node_id":"U_kgDOD-0LXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/267193182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex","html_url":"https://github.com/codex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"codex","id":267193182,"node_id":"U_kgDOD-0LXg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/267193182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex","html_url":"https://github.com/codex","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codex/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a37299b91bbbba7615d973ff8b9991a8365cafc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/a37299b91bbbba7615d973ff8b9991a8365cafc8","html_url":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/elenchus/commit/a37299b91bbbba7615d973ff8b9991a8365cafc8"}]},"status":"ahead","ahead_by":6,"behind_by":0,"total_commits":6,"commits":[{"sha":"961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38","node_id":"C_kwDOVws8odoAKDk2MWQzMjA5NmNiMmEwYjlhMmRjZWQ1MDM0MGFmNWNiY2RiMGZlMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:35:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:37:20Z"},"message":"Stop the fabricated repo in vercelIgnore.test.ts from repacking itself\n\nWhat broke. `npm test` failed 7 of 9 plain runs at 0faf606 with ENOTEMPTY\nfrom afterEach's rmSync in tests/vercelIgnore.test.ts, and 0 of 9 at\nddd9a37. The test file and web/scripts/vercel-ignore.mjs are identical in\nboth trees.\n\nHow it was shown. Each case builds a Git repository from web/, src/,\nscripts/ and tests/fixtures and commits it. `git commit` starts a detached\n`git maintenance run --auto`. Under Git 2.54 that repacks when objects/17\nholds two or more loose objects (crafted blobs: one does not trigger it, two\ndo). The fabricated repo holds one such object at ddd9a37 and at f7775c9,\nand two at 0faf606, so only the PR's bytes started a repack, which was still\nwriting .git/objects while the short cases removed the directory. GIT_TRACE\non the first commit shows `git repack -d -l --cruft` at the head and nothing\nat the merge-base.\n\nThe fix. The fabricated repo sets maintenance.auto=false and gc.auto=0\nafter init. With it, six plain runs of the full suite passed (950 of 950\neach, on a tree that also held this review's three added cases).\nWhat the cases assert is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"906d1c8a332ad04c9ec4403f158ebebfa24a1a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/trees/906d1c8a332ad04c9ec4403f158ebebfa24a1a07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/commits/961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38","html_url":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/elenchus/commit/961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38/comments","author":{"login":"claude","id":81847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"claude","id":81847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0faf606a131133e050b2b599b5d0cdf75e545c6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/0faf606a131133e050b2b599b5d0cdf75e545c6e","html_url":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/elenchus/commit/0faf606a131133e050b2b599b5d0cdf75e545c6e"}]},{"sha":"b275a564511c98b043e42fbb8003ccf9b79ee61a","node_id":"C_kwDOVws8odoAKGIyNzVhNTY0NTExYzk4YjA0M2U0MmZiYjgwMDNjY2Y5Yjc5ZWU2MWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:35:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:37:20Z"},"message":"Restore the power of two tests the clearing rewrote\n\nWhat broke. To keep the retired lens name out of the test sources, the\nduplicate-key case in tests/urlCodecs.test.ts was changed from\n`?lens=ledger&lens=broadcast` to `?lens=ledger&lens=ledger`. With two equal\nvalues the test passes whether canonicalSearch keeps the first duplicate or\nthe last. In tests/dom/theme.test.tsx the Broadcast step became\n`setDark(true); setDark(false); expect light` on Ledger, which ends where it\nstarted and passes with a listener that no longer follows the OS.\n\nHow it was shown. With `params.get(key)` swapped for\n`params.getAll(key).at(-1)`, tests/urlCodecs.test.ts passed 19 of 19 at\n0faf606 and failed at ddd9a37. With the OS-change handler returning early\noutside Poster, the PR's theme test passed 7 of 7.\n\nThe fix. The duplicate case uses two different surviving values in both\norders, and the theme test reads the root attribute after each OS change.\nBoth mutations now fail their test; unmutated, both files pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7de1a85e6bc0d45a69d0bdc4e645f6d133edaa42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/trees/7de1a85e6bc0d45a69d0bdc4e645f6d133edaa42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/commits/b275a564511c98b043e42fbb8003ccf9b79ee61a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/b275a564511c98b043e42fbb8003ccf9b79ee61a","html_url":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/elenchus/commit/b275a564511c98b043e42fbb8003ccf9b79ee61a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/b275a564511c98b043e42fbb8003ccf9b79ee61a/comments","author":{"login":"claude","id":81847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"claude","id":81847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38","html_url":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/elenchus/commit/961d32096cb2a0b9a2dced50340af5cbcdb0fe38"}]},{"sha":"9b3a90ad15c9d9cce7312d96e1753b58907a0a54","node_id":"C_kwDOVws8odoAKDliM2E5MGFkMTVjOWQ5Y2NlNzMxMmQ5NmUxNzUzYjU4OTA3YTBhNTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:35:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:37:20Z"},"message":"Pin the unset-kickoff and Brooklyn-day rules on the two remaining heroes\n\nWhat broke. The Broadcast ticker's DOM cases were the only tests that\nrendered a hero with a league-unset NEXT, and its selector cases the only\nones that checked a later-day NEXT against its Brooklyn date. Removing the\nticker removed them. The two heroes that stay, NextUpStrip and TonightSlate,\nwere rendered by one test, with exact times only.\n\nHow it was shown. With both heroes changed to print the filler instant as a\nclock for a placeholder kickoff, `npm test` passed 947 of 947, web's\n`npm test` 120 of 120, and typecheck was clean, at 0faf606.\n\nThe fix. Three cases in tests/dom/designCycle.test.tsx, on the real\n`upcoming` and `planSlate` selectors and the app's clock, with snapshot rows\npicked by position and overridden in memory: every Next-up card and its\noverflow line read TBC with no clock; the Poster slate row reads TBC and its\nsub-line names no time; a kickoff at 00:30 UTC is \"Tomorrow\" on Ledger and\n\"Sun 6 Sep\" on Poster, not the UTC date. Five mutations (card, overflow\nline, slate row, card date, slate title) each fail one of them.\ndocs/HONESTY.md rule 3 named the ticker; it now names what the heroes do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a967954b54a5c7d1dc32635181d916751d5ba91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/trees/1a967954b54a5c7d1dc32635181d916751d5ba91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/commits/9b3a90ad15c9d9cce7312d96e1753b58907a0a54","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/9b3a90ad15c9d9cce7312d96e1753b58907a0a54","html_url":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/elenchus/commit/9b3a90ad15c9d9cce7312d96e1753b58907a0a54","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/commits/9b3a90ad15c9d9cce7312d96e1753b58907a0a54/comments","author":{"login":"claude","id":81847,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/