250d5ca412151b55","node_id":"C_kwDOVws8odoAKGQxZjMyYzBkNDA0MzdkNTkyZTE1N2VhNDI1MGQ1Y2E0MTIxNTFiNTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:35:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","date":"2026-11-14T15:37:20Z"},"message":"Finish the two-lens wording the clearing missed\n\nWhat was wrong at 0faf606, each read against the code or measured:\n- README.md still said the football app is \"read through three visual\n  lenses\", two lines above a gallery of two.\n- TabNav's comment said the underline is \"floodlight in each lens\" (it is\n  pitch in both) and that the switcher cannot fit on the tab row at \"all\n  three phone widths\". Measured in Chrome on both production builds: the\n  row needs 331 px with Oswald loaded, so it wraps at 360 and fits at 375\n  (3.86 px spare) and 390 (18.86 px); with the fallback face it needs 394 px\n  and wraps at all three.\n- vite.config.ts still listed the marquee among what jsdom cannot check.\n- pr-comment.md asked for six 390 px captures; browser-matrix.md says four.\n- scripts/vercel-smoke.mjs still said every landmark is a receipt selector;\n  the Fixtures one no longer is.\n- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, which the README links as the current map, listed\n  the ticker, month cells, US broadcasters, a Broadcast-first theme, three\n  lens heroes and a `view` URL key. docs/README.md described it the same way.\n\nThe implementation prompt fenced docs/ as history (decision 6) and also said\ntext describing the current app changes with it (decision 7). ARCHITECTURE.md\nis a current description, so decision 7 governs it; the dated records under\ndocs/ are untouched. Comments and prose only: dist/ and web/.next/static are\nbyte-identical to the 0faf606 build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"774b585c7853366d3ee534d4dd13e4d04ad6100a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BeniCheni/elenchus/git/trees/774b585c7853366d3ee534d4dd1